{%- comment -%} ============================================================
  BBC DRAWING HERO v2 — the video hero for /pages/why-bamboo (2026-08-24,
  James: "pick a video and use claude design to build a hero with video").

  v1 was a LIGHT fabrication-drawing sheet (copy left, still photo right with
  dimension callouts). v2 joins the hero family established on home and impact
  in Aug 2026 — forest panel, copy on the shared --bbc-gutter axis, culm accent,
  media column right — with the two devices that stay UNIQUE to this page:
    · the drawing TITLE BLOCK survives as the eyebrow ("№ 02 — the material")
    · the DIMENSION CALLOUTS survive, pinned over the *moving* film — the
      fabrication-drawing language applied to live footage. Blocks unchanged,
      so positions stay editable in the theme editor.

  THE FILM: 42s cut from `video_frame_testing.mp4` in Shopify Files (the
  university frame-test footage): aluminium frame in the hydraulic rig →
  bamboo culm close-ups → the bamboo frame in the same rig → the sectioned
  culm. It is the page's argument — "a grass that rides like steel ... the
  material, measured" — told in footage. Presenter-to-camera stretches were
  deliberately cut around (they read badly with no sound).
  James asked for a YouTube pick; the channel's on-topic uploads were surveyed
  (choose-bamboo / notching / biocomposites) but YouTube rate-limits downloads
  on this connection to 360p, which is too soft for a hero — and the SAME
  footage family exists in Files at 720p. Swap the film by pasting a new URL
  into the "Film URL" setting.

  WHY THE CSS IS INLINE HERE, not in bbc-redesign-2026.css as v1 required:
  that file is re-emitted ~11x per page AFTER section styles, so class-level
  overrides silently lose (documented cascade trap, project CLAUDE.md #1).
  v2 uses a fresh .dvh-* namespace that NO other stylesheet mentions — the
  cascade war cannot reach names it does not use. bbc-align.css still owns the
  shared --bbc-gutter variable via the .bbc-rd wrapper class.
  EXCEPTION FOUND ON DEPLOY: element-level estate rules (h1, h1 em, .rd-btn
  variants keyed to this page's OLD light surface) still reach INTO the
  namespace via shared tags/classes — those three get scoped !important
  re-assertions below, each annotated.

  PLAYBACK pattern copied from the impact hero (load() + start on canplay +
  fade in only on `playing`) — play() resolving while still paused shipped as
  a real bug on the homepage hero; do not simplify this. Gates: reduced
  motion, phones, save-data → the still photo stays.
============================================================ {%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'bbc-redesign-2026.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign film = section.settings.video_url
  assign poster = section.settings.video_poster
-%}

<div class="bbc-rd dvh-wrap">
  <div class="dvh">
    <div class="dvh-copy">
      {%- if section.settings.crumb_label != blank -%}
        <nav class="rd-crumb dvh-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span class="rd-sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">{{ section.settings.crumb_label }}</span>
        </nav>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.tb_v1 != blank -%}
        <p class="dvh-tb"><span class="dvh-tb-k">{{ section.settings.tb_k1 | default: 'drawing' }}</span> {{ section.settings.tb_v1 }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h1 class="dvh-h1">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.cta1_label != blank or section.settings.cta2_label != blank -%}
        <div class="dvh-cta">
          {%- if section.settings.cta1_label != blank -%}
            <a class="rd-btn rd-lime" href="{{ section.settings.cta1_url | default: '#' }}">{{ section.settings.cta1_label }} <span class="rd-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.cta2_label != blank -%}
            <a class="rd-btn rd-on-dark" href="{{ section.settings.cta2_url | default: '#' }}">{{ section.settings.cta2_label }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.lede != blank -%}
        <p class="dvh-lede">{{ section.settings.lede }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="dvh-media">
      {%- comment -%} The still photo ALWAYS renders and carries the alt text;
        the film layers over it and fades in only once genuinely playing, so
        every failure mode degrades to the photo, never to a black box. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
        <img class="dvh-img" src="{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
             srcset="{{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w, {{ section.settings.image | image_url: width: 1400 }} 1400w"
             sizes="(max-width:1199px) 100vw, 55vw"
             alt="{{ section.settings.image_alt | escape }}"
             width="{{ section.settings.image.width }}" height="{{ section.settings.image.height }}" fetchpriority="high">
      {%- else -%}
        <img class="dvh-img" src="{{ section.settings.image_fallback | default: 'bbc-rd-frame-build.jpg' | asset_url }}"
             alt="{{ section.settings.image_alt | escape }}" width="1400" height="1050" fetchpriority="high">
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if film != blank -%}
        <video class="dvh-film" muted loop playsinline webkit-playsinline preload="metadata"
               {% if poster != blank %}poster="{{ poster }}"{% endif %}
               aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" src="{{ film }}"></video>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="dvh-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      {%- comment -%} Callouts are gated OFF by default (2026-08-24, James: "there is a
        hardcoded culm 30-40mm check on the hero, can you remove"). The chip was the saved
        c1 block rendering over the film. Gated rather than deleted so his saved block and
        its editor controls survive intact - flip "Show dimension callouts" to bring the
        device back. Default false works because the draft template has no show_callouts
        key, so the schema default genuinely applies (the `| default:` gating bug only
        bites saved-as-empty strings, not absent keys). {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_callouts -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.type == 'callout' and block.settings.text != blank -%}
            <span class="dvh-callout" style="top:{{ block.settings.top | default: 30 }}%;left:{{ block.settings.left | default: 34 }}%" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ block.settings.text }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
  {%- if section.settings.show_nodediv -%}
    <div class="rd-nodediv" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
/* .dvh-* is a fresh namespace on purpose — see the head comment. Shared things
   (buttons, breadcrumb, node divider, --bbc-gutter) come from the estate. */
.dvh{display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.82fr 1fr;align-items:stretch;min-height:clamp(560px,82vh,940px);min-height:clamp(560px,82svh,940px);background:var(--forest,#003C32);overflow:hidden;isolation:isolate}
.dvh-copy{position:relative;z-index:3;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;padding:clamp(26px,4.8vh,80px) clamp(20px,2.6vw,48px) clamp(30px,5.4vh,84px) var(--bbc-gutter,clamp(32px,6vw,120px));container-type:inline-size}
/* the culm, MATERIAL-PAGE variant: same device as home/impact but with a tighter
   16+4px node period — culms carry their nodes closest near the base, and this is
   the page about the plant. Pseudo-element, so Dawn's div:empty trap cannot bite. */
.dvh-copy::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:calc(var(--bbc-gutter,48px) - 34px);top:13%;bottom:13%;width:3px;border-radius:3px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom,var(--lime,#D4FD62) 0 16px,rgba(6,35,28,.55) 16px 20px)}
.dvh-crumb{margin-bottom:clamp(12px,2vh,22px)}
.dvh-crumb,.dvh-crumb a{color:rgba(230,220,200,.72)!important;text-shadow:none}
.dvh-crumb a:hover{color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)!important}
.dvh-crumb [aria-current]{color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)}
.dvh-tb{margin:0 0 clamp(10px,1.8vh,20px);font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)}
.dvh-tb-k{display:inline-block;margin-right:10px;padding:2px 8px;border:1.5px solid rgba(212,253,98,.5);border-radius:3px;color:rgba(230,220,200,.85)}
/* colour needs the same armour as the em below: the page's estate sheets style h1
   for the OLD light drawing-sheet (near-forest ink) at >= (0,1,2)+, and they load
   after the section bundle - on the deployed page the headline rendered DARK on the
   forest panel (caught by screenshot). Scoped !important, nothing else uses .dvh-*. */
.dvh .dvh-h1{margin:0;color:var(--bone,#E6DCC8)!important;font-size:clamp(2.3rem,7vw,5.4rem);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.01em;text-wrap:balance}
/* .dvh .dvh-h1 em + !important: an estate rule styles `h1 em` at (0,1,2) with a mid
   green (#3F8B66) and the section stylesheet bundle loads BEFORE the 11x re-emitted
   global files, so a bare .dvh-h1 em (0,1,1) lost on both counts - caught on the
   deployed page, the em rendered pine instead of lime. */
.dvh .dvh-h1 em{font-style:italic;color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)!important}
.dvh-lede{margin:clamp(14px,2.2vh,24px) 0 0;max-width:46ch;color:rgba(238,243,236,.92);font-size:clamp(1rem,1.9cqw,1.25rem);line-height:1.55}
.dvh-cta{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;margin-top:clamp(18px,2.8vh,30px)}
/* same story for the primary button: an estate rule keyed to this page's old light
   surface repainted .rd-lime as a dark pill with dark text (screenshot-caught,
   unreadable). Re-assert the lime pair inside .dvh only. */
.dvh .dvh-cta .rd-btn.rd-lime{background:var(--lime,#D4FD62)!important;color:var(--forest,#003C32)!important;border-color:var(--lime,#D4FD62)!important}
.dvh .dvh-cta .rd-btn.rd-on-dark{color:var(--bone,#E6DCC8)!important;border-color:rgba(230,220,200,.65)!important;background:transparent!important}
.dvh-media{position:relative;z-index:1;min-height:0;overflow:hidden}
.dvh-img,.dvh-film{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block}
.dvh-film{opacity:0;transition:opacity .6s ease;z-index:1}
.dvh-film.is-on{opacity:1}
.dvh-scrim{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:2;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--forest,#003C32) 0%,rgba(0,60,50,.34) 28%,rgba(0,60,50,0) 64%);pointer-events:none}
/* dimension callout, the drawing device over the film. Forest chip on lime text —
   measured over the brightest rig footage the pale variant fell under 3:1.
   Currently gated OFF by the show_callouts setting - styles kept for re-enable. */
.dvh-callout{position:absolute;z-index:3;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);padding:5px 10px;border:1.5px solid rgba(212,253,98,.55);border-radius:4px;background:rgba(0,40,33,.72);color:var(--lime,#D4FD62);font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.06em;white-space:nowrap}
.dvh-callout::after{content:"";position:absolute;left:50%;top:100%;width:1.5px;height:22px;background:rgba(212,253,98,.55)}
@media(min-width:1200px){
  .dvh .dvh-h1{font-size:clamp(2.4rem,min(13cqw,8vh),5.6rem)}
}
@media(max-width:1199px){
  .dvh{grid-template-columns:1fr;min-height:0}
  .dvh-media{grid-row:1;height:clamp(260px,42svh,480px)}
  .dvh-copy{grid-row:2;padding-block:clamp(28px,5vw,56px)}
  .dvh-copy::before{position:relative;inset:auto;width:68px;height:3px;margin:0 0 18px;background:repeating-linear-gradient(to right,var(--lime,#D4FD62) 0 16px,rgba(6,35,28,.55) 16px 20px)}
  .dvh-scrim{background:linear-gradient(0deg,var(--forest,#003C32) 0%,rgba(0,60,50,.32) 26%,rgba(0,60,50,0) 62%)}
}
@media(max-width:749px){
  .dvh-media{height:clamp(210px,32svh,380px)}
  /* action above the explanation on phones — the family rule. DOM order intact. */
  .dvh-copy{display:flex}
  .dvh-crumb{order:1}
  .dvh-tb{order:2}
  .dvh-h1{order:3}
  .dvh-cta{order:4;margin-top:clamp(16px,2.4vh,24px)}
  .dvh-lede{order:5;margin-top:clamp(16px,2.4vh,24px)}
  .dvh-callout{display:none} /* pins mislead at phone crops; the film reads alone */
}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .dvh-film{display:none}
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
/* Why-bamboo hero film. Same hardened pattern as the impact hero: play() can
   resolve while the element is still paused at t=0, so start on `canplay` and
   reveal only on `playing`. Gates leave the still photo in place. */
(function () {
  var v = document.querySelector('.dvh-film');
  if (!v) return;
  if (window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
  /* phone gate removed 2026-08-24 - James: hero films must play on mobile too */
  var conn = navigator.connection || navigator.mozConnection || navigator.webkitConnection;
  if (conn && (conn.saveData || /(^|-)2g$/.test(conn.effectiveType || ''))) return;
  v.muted = true; v.defaultMuted = true;
  function start() {
    var p = v.play();
    if (p && p.catch) p.catch(function () { /* autoplay refused — photo stays */ });
  }
  v.addEventListener('playing', function () { v.classList.add('is-on'); }, { once: true });
  v.setAttribute('preload', 'auto');
  v.load();
  if (v.readyState >= 3) start();
  else v.addEventListener('canplay', start, { once: true });
  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () {
    if (document.hidden) { v.pause(); }
    else if (v.classList.contains('is-on')) { start(); }
  });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "BBC Drawing hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "bbc-drawing-hero-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Breadcrumb" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "crumb_label", "label": "Breadcrumb label", "default": "Why Bamboo" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Title block (drawing panel)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tb_k1", "label": "Row 1 label", "default": "drawing" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tb_v1", "label": "Row 1 value", "default": "№ 02 — the material" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tb_k2", "label": "Row 2 label (unused in v2, kept for saved data)", "default": "drawn" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tb_v2", "label": "Row 2 value (unused in v2, kept for saved data)", "default": "by hand, since 2012" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Content" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading (use <em> for the tinted words)", "default": "a grass that rides like steel" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "lede", "label": "Lede", "default": "Every workshop opens with the same question. It sounds like a gimmick — until day one is over. This is the material, measured." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta1_label", "label": "Primary CTA label", "default": "read the datasheet" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta1_url", "label": "Primary CTA link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta2_label", "label": "Secondary CTA label", "default": "build one" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "cta2_url", "label": "Secondary CTA link" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Film (looping, silent)" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "video_url", "label": "Film URL (mp4, Shopify Files)", "default": "https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/cdb602478fe441388ed3efc045ede4f6.mp4", "info": "42s frame-test cut. Paste a different Files mp4 URL to swap. Clear to show the still photo only." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "video_poster", "label": "Poster image URL", "default": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0502/8695/2631/files/preview_images/cdb602478fe441388ed3efc045ede4f6.thumbnail.0000000000.jpg?v=1787563117" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Still image (fallback + phones)" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_fallback", "label": "Fallback asset filename", "default": "bbc-rd-frame-build.jpg" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "image_alt", "label": "Image alt text", "default": "A bamboo bicycle frame clamped in its building jig" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Devices" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_nodediv", "label": "Node-divider seam at the base", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_callouts", "label": "Show dimension callouts over the film", "default": false, "info": "The pinned drawing-style labels (e.g. culm diameter). Off by default — James 2026-08-24." }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "name": "Dimension callout",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Label", "default": "culm · 30–40 mm ø" },
        { "type": "range", "id": "top", "label": "Position from top (%)", "min": 5, "max": 90, "step": 1, "unit": "%", "default": 30 },
        { "type": "range", "id": "left", "label": "Position from left (%)", "min": 10, "max": 80, "step": 1, "unit": "%", "default": 30 }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "BBC Drawing hero",
      "blocks": [ { "type": "callout" }, { "type": "callout" } ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
